=== moonbit-crdt ===

[1] G-Counter — disjoint increments merge cleanly
  A = A=3 (value 3)
  B = B=5 (value 5)
  merged = A=3;B=5 (value 8)
  -> no increment is lost, and the merge is order-independent

[2] PN-Counter — increments and decrements coexist
  state = p=A=10|n=A=4
  value = 6 (10 increments - 4 decrements)

[3] OR-Set — a concurrent add wins, but an observed removal is durable
  canonical form = <live dots>|<tombstoned dots>|<dot counters>
  (a) add-wins — B removed the dot it had seen; A added a dot B never saw
      A          = lamp=A#0,A#1||A=2
      B          = lamp=|lamp=A#0|A=1
      merged     = lamp=A#1|lamp=A#0|A=2
      contains   = true  <- the concurrent add won

  (b) durable removal — A removed a dot it had observed; B still holds it
      A          = desk=|desk=A#0|A=1
      B (stale)  = desk=A#0||A=1
      merged     = desk=|desk=A#0|A=1
      contains   = false / false  <- not resurrected

[4] LWW-Register — concurrent writes, deterministic winner
  A writes "light" at t=1000
  B writes "dark"  at t=2000
  merged value = dark
  (the same winner is chosen no matter which side merges first)

Every merge above is commutative, associative and idempotent,
under the preconditions stated in the README (distinct node ids,
each replica writing only its own counter key).
see crdt_test.mbt and the differential harness in tools/.
